From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:01:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Set the dGPU power before the RAM init

The EC powers the dGPU on at power-up, and its PMH7 keeps the state of
the boot before across a warm reset. mb_late_romstage_setup() set it as
the "enable_dual_graphics" option asks only after the RAM init, so with
the dGPU disabled every training after a power-up ran with the dGPU
powered, and every training after a warm reset without it, while the
board always runs with it off.

On a ThinkPad W541 with four DIMMs (native RAM init) the reads of
channel 1 came out 2 to 4 PI ticks and 5 to 9 Vref steps narrower after
every power-up than after every warm reset (7 of 7 against 12 of 12),
two margins at or below the retrain limit; with the dGPU powered on
from the OS before a warm reset they came out as narrow, with it off as
wide (4 of 4). Nothing done within the boot recovered them: the dGPU
stays powered through the whole RAM init.

Add mb_pre_raminit_setup(), right before the RAM init (both the native
one and mrc.bin), and set the dGPU power there; the dGPU device is
still hidden after it. The hook is declared in raminit.h, which the
version of the saved native training follows, so the boards train once
again in the new conditions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ie108f0b063f364eec3aa1b6091beb31e9d86e573
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c  | 21 ++++++++++++++++-----
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h  | 10 ++++++++++
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
index f786f68bf5..bf77d97ead 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #include <option.h>
 #include <ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.h>
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
-#include <romstage_handoff.h>
+#include <northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h>
 
 void mainboard_config_rcba(void)
 {
@@ -20,7 +20,16 @@ void mainboard_config_rcba(void)
 	RCBA16(D20IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQA, PIRQB, PIRQC, PIRQD);
 }
 
-void mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
+/*
+ * The dGPU as the option wants it before the RAM init, not after it: the EC
+ * powers the dGPU on at power-up and keeps the state of the boot before
+ * across a warm reset. With it powered during the training and turned off
+ * after, the trainings after a power-up were measured with a noise the board
+ * does not run with: on a W541 the reads of channel 1 came out 2 to 4 PI ticks
+ * and 5 to 9 Vref steps narrower than after a warm reset, every time, and as
+ * narrow after a warm reset with the dGPU powered from the OS.
+ */
+void mb_pre_raminit_setup(bool s3resume)
 {
 	u8 enable_peg = get_uint_option("enable_dual_graphics", 0);
 
@@ -29,8 +38,7 @@ void mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
 	 * suspending: keep that state on S3 resume, the power resource _STA
 	 * reports it and the OS powers the GPU back on when it needs it.
 	 */
-	bool keep_state = CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM) && enable_peg &&
-			  romstage_handoff_is_resume();
+	bool keep_state = CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM) && enable_peg && s3resume;
 
 	if (!keep_state) {
 		bool power_en = pmh7_dgpu_power_state();
@@ -38,8 +46,11 @@ void mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
 		if (enable_peg != power_en)
 			pmh7_dgpu_power_enable(!power_en);
 	}
+}
 
-	if (!enable_peg) {
+void mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
+{
+	if (!get_uint_option("enable_dual_graphics", 0)) {
 		// Hide disabled dGPU device
 		pci_and_config32(HOST_BRIDGE, DEVEN, ~DEVEN_D1F0EN);
 	}
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h
index b1f30909e3..6eee092240 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h
@@ -18,6 +18,16 @@ struct spd_info {
 /* Mainboard callback to fill in the SPD addresses */
 void mb_get_spd_map(struct spd_info *spdi);
 
+/*
+ * Mainboard callback, optional, right before the RAM init: put the board in the
+ * state it runs in, as far as the memory sees it. The training is measured in
+ * the conditions of this moment and kept for every boot after it: on a ThinkPad
+ * W541 a dGPU left powered by the EC at power-up, then turned off after the RAM
+ * init, made every training after a power-up narrower in the reads of channel 1
+ * (2 to 4 PI ticks, 5 to 9 Vref steps) than the board runs with.
+ */
+void mb_pre_raminit_setup(bool s3resume);
+
 void get_spd_info(struct spd_info *spdi, const struct northbridge_intel_haswell_config *cfg);
 const uint8_t *get_spd_from_cbfs(struct spd_info *spdi);
 void report_memory_config(void);
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
index 0c4814d6c6..1386eb55c2 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -118,6 +118,10 @@ void __weak mb_late_romstage_setup(void)
 {
 }
 
+void __weak mb_pre_raminit_setup(bool s3resume)
+{
+}
+
 /* The romstage entry point for this platform is not mainboard-specific, hence the name */
 void mainboard_romstage_entry(void)
 {
@@ -176,6 +180,8 @@ void mainboard_romstage_entry(void)
 	if (CONFIG(INTEL_TXT))
 		intel_txt_romstage_init();
 
+	mb_pre_raminit_setup(s3resume);
+
 	perform_raminit(s3resume);
 
 	post_code(0x3c);
